---
// Bento visitor tracking. Shared by MainLayout and LandingLayout so the site
// UUID lives in one place, matching GoogleAnalytics.astro.
//
// The loader auto-fires a pageview on its own — verified against production,
// where it produces `POST track.bentonow.com/tracking/events -> 201`. That is
// why there is no inline `bento.view()` call here.
//
// There used to be one, guarded by `if (typeof(bento$) != 'undefined')`. That
// guard could never pass: it ran during parse, while the `async defer` loader
// above it had definitionally not executed yet, so `bento$` was always
// undefined. It was dead code — but removing it does NOT disable tracking,
// because the loader was never depending on it.
//
// Deliberately ungated, unlike GA4: Bento ties visits to email subscribers, and
// adding a PROD/hostname guard here would be a behavioural change beyond
// restoring what production already does. Worth revisiting separately if
// staging traffic turns out to be polluting the Bento data.
const BENTO_SITE_UUID = "57d9b8196b2b704a30da5ac245bf2cfe";
---

<script src={`https://fast.bentonow.com?site_uuid=${BENTO_SITE_UUID}&js=true`} async defer></script>
